 ],
 "sentences": [
  "Each moment like that could let it rise a little.",
  "Fractions of an inch.",
  "Across one hundred and fifty-four flights, it walked itself upward.",
  "It left a record of the climb: parallel lines of dust, dirt and petroleum jelly along the seal, marking its steps.",
  "From the outside, the change at its lower edge was about half an inch.",
  "Too small, the N - T - S - B found, to catch on a walk-around.",
  "On the fifth of January, climbing out of Portland, the plug reached the top of its stops.",
  "The pins rode up off the pads.",
  "The upper fittings struck their rollers and split.",
  "The lower hinges twisted.",
  "And the plug left the airplane: up, out—and back."
 ],
